            <ArticleTitle>[Double aneurysm occurring on a venous aortocoronary graft].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1213-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report the case of a 48-year old patient admitted to hospital for unstable angina 13 years after primary myocardial revascularisation by a saphenous vein aorto-coronary bypass graft. Routine chest X-ray showed a left para-hilar opacity which CT scan and angiography confirmed to be aneurysmal and pseudoaneurysmal dilatations of the saphenous vein bypass graft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
